---
import Case from '../../layouts/Case.astro';
import CaseSection from '../../components/case/CaseSection.astro';
import ThemeLab from '../../components/ThemeLab';
import PanceShowcase from '../../components/PanceShowcase.astro';
import { auditFindings, decisions, facts, libraryStats, pance, qualityGates, releases } from '../../data/pance';
import { formatCount, spellOut } from '../../lib/format';
---

<Case
  slug="pance"
  title="Pance Design System"
  headline="One source of truth,"
  headlineAccent="from Figma to npm."
  summary="Pance is an open-source design system for social-impact and data-heavy products. I took it from a generated docs site to a tested, versioned system with a Figma library, React components and tokens on npm."
  description={`Case study: how Jonathan Lerma built Pance, an accessible, token-driven design system — ${facts.tokens} tokens, ${formatCount(facts.figmaVariants)} Figma variants, WCAG 2.2 AA tested in CI, published on npm.`}
  meta={[
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Creator & maintainer — design, engineering, docs' },
    { label: 'Year', value: '2026' },
    { label: 'Stack', value: 'W3C DTCG tokens · React 19 · Tailwind v4 · Figma variables · GitHub Actions' },
    { label: 'Licence', value: `MIT · v${pance.version}` },
  ]}
  links={[
    { label: 'Documentation', href: pance.docs },
    { label: 'GitHub', href: pance.repo },
    { label: 'npm', href: pance.npmReact },
    { label: 'Figma Community', href: pance.figma },
  ]}
>
  <CaseSection id="try" number="01" eyebrow="Try it" title="Change the brand." accent="Nothing else.">
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      These are the published @pance/react components. Pick a ramp and one attribute re-points every token that aliases
      it, in light and dark.
    </Fragment>
    <ThemeLab client:visible />
    <p class="mono">Tip: switch the site to light mode from the top bar — the same components follow.</p>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection
    id="problem"
    number="02"
    eyebrow="The problem"
    title="It looked finished."
    accent="It wasn’t a system yet."
  >
    <p>
      Pance began as a documentation site generated with Figma Make. The pages were polished, but the components didn’t
      read from tokens, the docs and the code disagreed, and some of what looked right was failing accessibility in ways
      you can’t see.
    </p>
    <p>
      So before building anything new, I extracted it into a repo and wrote an audit: what the docs say, what the code
      does, and a fix for each gap. Some of what it found:
    </p>
    <div class="cards">
      {auditFindings.map((finding) => (
        <div>
          <p class="mono">{finding.label}</p>
          <h3 class="quote card-figure">{finding.value}</h3>
          <p>{finding.text}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p>
      Docs and code also disagreed on the basics: the breakpoint (480 vs. 640 px), the H3 size (18 vs. 20 px), disabled
      opacity (four different values). Each one became a recorded decision.
    </p>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection id="arch" number="03" eyebrow="Architecture" title="Three tiers," accent="five outputs.">
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      A change starts in one JSON file and reaches design and code in the same pull request.
    </Fragment>
    <figure class="flow" aria-label="How a token change flows through Pance">
      <ol class="flow-tiers">
        <li>
          <span class="mono">Tier 1</span>
          <b>Primitives</b>
          <small>aqua.700 = #0e7490</small>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="mono">Tier 2</span>
          <b>Semantic</b>
          <small>intent.primary.solid → aqua.700</small>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="mono">Tier 3</span>
          <b>Components</b>
          <small>button.primary.bg → intent.primary.solid</small>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <ul class="flow-out">
        <li>
          <b>CSS variables</b>
          <small>--pance-color-*, light + dark</small>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Tailwind v4 theme</b>
          <small>bg-primary-solid, text-ink-muted</small>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Typed JS object</b>
          <small>charts, canvas, tests</small>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Figma variables</b>
          <small>{facts.figmaVariables}, Light and Dark modes</small>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>@pance/react</b>
          <small>{facts.reactComponents} components on npm</small>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <figcaption>
        {facts.tokens} tokens in the W3C DTCG format. Components may only read semantic or component tokens —{' '}
        <code>lint:tokens</code> fails the build otherwise.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection id="decisions" number="04" eyebrow="Decisions" title="Written down," accent="so they last.">
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      Pance keeps a register of design decision records (DDR-DS). A future contributor can read why something is the way
      it is — and argue with it.
    </Fragment>
    <div class="cards">
      {decisions.map((decision) => (
        <div>
          <p class="mono">{decision.id}</p>
          <h3>{decision.title}</h3>
          <p>{decision.text}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection
    id="quality"
    number="05"
    eyebrow="Quality"
    title="Accessibility checked"
    accent="by machines,"
    after="every push."
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">Memory and good intentions don’t scale. CI does.</Fragment>
    <dl class="gates">
      {qualityGates.map((gate) => (
        <div>
          <dt>{gate.name}</dt>
          <dd>{gate.text}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
    <p>
      Every interactive control also gets at least a 24 × 24 px target (WCAG 2.5.8) through an invisible hit area, and
      panels like popovers and date pickers shift to stay inside the viewport.
    </p>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection id="product" number="06" eyebrow="Built for data" title="Charts and tables" accent="are first-class.">
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      Metric cards, line, bar, diverging, heatmap, donut and scatter charts, meters and a data table with expandable
      rows — each with a table view for screen readers.
    </Fragment>
    <PanceShowcase />
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection
    id="ship"
    number="07"
    eyebrow="Shipping"
    title={`${spellOut(releases.length)} releases,`}
    accent="no stored secrets."
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      Published from GitHub Actions with npm trusted publishing and provenance. The docs deploy to GitHub Pages on every
      push to main.
    </Fragment>
    <ol class="timeline">
      {releases.map((release) => (
        <li>
          <b>{release.version}</b>
          <span>{release.text}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <ul class="stats">
      {libraryStats.map((stat) => (
        <li>
          <b>{stat.value}</b>
          <span>{stat.label}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection id="next" number="08" eyebrow="What’s next" title="Proof in" accent="real products.">
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li>
        <strong>Altazor CRM</strong> — the first production app built on Pance, for a creative writing school.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Screen-reader passes</strong> with NVDA and VoiceOver on the dialog, combobox, data table and date
        picker.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Figma Code Connect</strong>, and dark values for component tokens in Figma.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>This website.</strong> It’s built with @pance/react and @pance/tokens plus a thin editorial layer: a
        display typeface, re-pointed font tokens and a generated brand scope. Press <kbd>I</kbd> to see it.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </CaseSection>
</Case>

<style>
  .flow {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .flow-tiers,
  .flow-out {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .flow-tiers {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }
  .flow-out {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
  }
  .flow li {
    padding: 18px;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: var(--glass-fill);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-edge), var(--elev-1);
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .flow-tiers li {
    box-shadow:
      var(--glass-edge),
      inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--pance-color-aqua-400) 30%, transparent),
      var(--elev-2),
      0 24px 50px -30px color-mix(in srgb, var(--pance-color-aqua-500) 50%, transparent);
  }
  .flow-tiers li + li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    left: -12px;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    color: var(--brand);
  }
  .flow b {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .flow small {
    font: 500 0.75rem/1.4 var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .flow-arrow {
    height: 36px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .flow-arrow::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 10%;
    right: 10%;
    top: 0;
    height: 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-top: 0;
    border-radius: 0 0 14px 14px;
  }
  .flow-arrow::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 18px;
    width: 1px;
    height: 18px;
    background: var(--line);
  }
  .flow figcaption {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .flow code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--brand);
  }
  .gates {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0 28px;
  }
  .gates div {
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .gates dt {
    font: 500 0.8rem/1 var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--brand);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .gates dd {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .flow-tiers {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .flow-tiers li + li::before {
      left: 50%;
      top: -6px;
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(90deg);
    }
    .flow-out {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
    .gates {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
